# Notebook policy

Notebooks are for narrative EDA and reporting. They must not contain reusable
business logic.

- Import from `perp_lab.*`; do not define analysis functions inline. If you need
  a new transformation, add it to `src/perp_lab/` (with a test) and import it.
- Load data from `data/validated` or `data/processed` parquet; never re-download
  or mutate raw data in a notebook.
- Never touch the frozen holdout partition in an EDA notebook.
- Each analysis cell follows: Question -> Method -> Result -> Figure/Table ->
  Interpretation -> Implication for strategy/methodology.
- Strip outputs before committing (`nbstripout`) to keep diffs reviewable.
